                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "86ceb0e6-b66e-38d0-ad77-2b6ac91fdd4b",
                        "entry_id": "f91cbe2b-4320-338e-9612-ae93732c701f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Pertaining to values or properties approached at infinity."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ee28a08f-88c0-4b91-8218-08b481b03662",
                                "sense_id": "86ceb0e6-b66e-38d0-ad77-2b6ac91fdd4b",
                                "text": "F. Skof investigated an interesting asymptotic property of the additive functions (see Theorem 2.34). In fact, she proved that a function f : E₁ → E₂ is additive if and only if ‖f(x + y) − f(x) − f(y)‖ → 0 as ‖x‖ + ‖y‖ → ∞, where E₁ is a normed space and E₂ is a Banach space."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9ef3a22d-0653-4d12-b3ad-b60b4e38bec7",
                                "sense_id": "86ceb0e6-b66e-38d0-ad77-2b6ac91fdd4b",
                                "text": "More recently, a direction of research initiated by Macpherson and Steinhorn [28] and continued by Elwes [13, 14] and Ryten studies classes of finite structures in which definable sets have a uniform asymptotic behaviour, as the cardinalities of the universes increase."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a13dd3eb-5c8a-307c-8311-7799dead8137",
                        "entry_id": "f91cbe2b-4320-338e-9612-ae93732c701f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Coming into consideration as a variable tends to a limit, usually infinity."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4591b728-5038-4444-bfe0-79504bb0a48f",
                                "sense_id": "a13dd3eb-5c8a-307c-8311-7799dead8137",
                                "text": "Because for some transwomen, femininity can feel asymptotic — the closer you get, the more you feel you can never make it."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "be67f40f-f954-4045-9537-840c96fe3848",
                                "sense_id": "a13dd3eb-5c8a-307c-8311-7799dead8137",
                                "text": "The asymptotic behavior of a function"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
